      "margin_number": 206,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "As well as having second person imperatives, which you have already met, Greek has third person imperative forms. Third person imperatives do not exist in English, but their nearest equivalent is ‘let him/her –’, ‘let them –’, etc. Here are the imperative forms of παύω in full, with the third person imperatives taking their place beside the second persons:",
